# xhcitr-imports.allow - every function XHCITR.EXE and XHCITR64.EXE import,
# by architecture and module (check-imports.ps1 holds each image to its rows
# exactly: an import not listed fails, and so does a row the image no
# longer imports). A module name alone would let through a function only
# NT exports, and XHCITR.EXE would then not start on Windows 98 SE.
#
# Where the rows come from: the 3.4.1.0 release images' import tables, read
# with check-imports.ps1 -List, and the one function this tree's images
# import beyond them, USER32's IntersectRect (the main window's placement
# check), which the installer window XHCIWIZ.EXE imports too
# (xhciinst\xhciinst-imports.allow's x86 window rows). The x86 rows are the
# Windows 98 SE baseline: XHCITR.EXE of that cycle started and ran on 98 SE
# (runs/run-46.md), and so did XHCIWIZ.EXE. The amd64 rows are XHCITR64's,
# whose ceiling is XP x64. A new x86 row needs the function in Windows 98
# SE's export table of that module first (a run-time lookup, GetProcAddress,
# needs no row); a new amd64 row needs it in XP x64's. COMCTL32's import
# library binds InitCommonControls by ordinal, listed as #17.
#
# arch  module        function

